{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1903","published":"2026-04-11T11:10:55Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:55.316823729Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-67724","CVE-2026-35536"],"summary":"python-tornado security update","details":"Tornado is an open source version of the scalable, non-blocking web server and tools.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nTornado is a Python web framework and asynchronous networking library. In versions 6.5.2 and below, the supplied reason phrase is used unescaped in HTTP headers (where it could be used for header injection) or in HTML in the default error page (where it could be used for XSS) and can be exploited by passing untrusted or malicious data into the reason argument. Used by both RequestHandler.set_status and tornado.web.HTTPError, the argument is designed to allow applications to pass custom &quot;reason&quot; phrases (the &quot;Not Found&quot; in HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found) to the HTTP status line (mainly for non-standard status codes). This issue is fixed in version 6.5.3.(CVE-2025-67724)\n\nIn Tornado before 6.5.5, cookie attribute injection could occur because the domain, path, and samesite arguments to .RequestHandler.set_cookie were not checked for crafted characters.(CVE-2026-35536)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python-tornado","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/python-tornado&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.5-4.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["python-tornado-debuginfo-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","python-tornado-debugsource-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","python-tornado-help-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","python3-tornado-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["python-tornado-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["python-tornado-debuginfo-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","python-tornado-debugsource-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","python-tornado-help-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","python3-tornado-6.5-4.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm"]},"databa